    "body": "At `ca864ff`, the separate `deepcopy` calls break a reference needed by enabled relative-action processors. `AbsoluteActionsProcessorStep.relative_step` must point to the relative step used by that worker's preprocessor. Copying them independently creates two different relative steps.\n\nA minimal reduction using the PR's processor classes:\n\n```python\nfrom copy import deepcopy\nimport torch\nfrom lerobot.processor import AbsoluteActionsProcessorStep, RelativeActionsProcessorStep\n\nrelative = RelativeActionsProcessorStep(enabled=True)\nabsolute = AbsoluteActionsProcessorStep(enabled=True, relative_step=relative)\npre, post = deepcopy(relative), deepcopy(absolute)\n\npre({\"observation\": {\"observation.state\": torch.tensor([[10.0]])}})\nassert post.relative_step is not pre\npost({\"action\": torch.tensor([[1.0]])})  # raises: no state has been cached\n```\n\nIf the original relative step already cached state `100`, the copied postprocessor instead returns `101`, without an error, after its worker's preprocessor sees state `10`. The required target is `11`.\n\nThe context can be copied in one pass so the shared `deepcopy` memo preserves these connections within a worker:\n\n```python\nctx = deepcopy(\n    (policy, env_preprocessor, env_postprocessor, preprocessor, postprocessor)\n)\n```\n\nI checked the PR's selected helper and processor definitions on CPU with a scripted task callback. The separate-copy version fails the fresh-state, cached-state, same-worker reuse and two-worker reuse controls; the single-copy candidate passes those and the disabled-processor and uncopyable-policy controls. The existing tests use identity processors and replace `eval_one`, so they do not exercise the paired steps.\n\nThis is a bounded source-level check, not a full `eval_policy_all`, GPU or robot run. A regression using the real paired pipelines would protect this relationship when the PR is rebased. The per-worker weight-memory cost remains a separate trade-off.",
    "body_sha256": "f895c46709a3c3c093bd6b03be007126b31e95ebfebaf6699ac1a8369d2e797c",
    "precheck": "PR still open at the same head; issue comments, reviews and review comments empty. Verified authenticated identity before posting.",
    "new_review_count": 1,
    "repository_commits_published": 0
  },
